    "public_api_change": "ADDITIVE",
    "schema_diff_summary": "document.rs has one test module named tests. Add the new test function at the end of that module, before its closing brace. Do not write a second mod tests. Add is_execution on impl MarkKind. Keep it public, the same way is_bookmark is public. Do not add a dead_code attribute. The body is matches!(self, Self::Execution). Do not write if self == Self::Execution { true } else { false }. Do not write two if arms that return the same value. Combine them with ||. That is clippy::if_same_then_else. Do not touch is_breakpoint, is_diagnostic, is_bookmark, reload_choice, or reload_prompt_line. The existing tests a_breakpoint_kind_is_a_breakpoint, a_warning_kind_is_a_diagnostic, and a_bookmark_kind_is_a_bookmark stay green. Do not rewrite their assertions. The test an_execution_kind_is_an_execution checks MarkKind::Execution is true. MarkKind::Bookmark is false. MarkKind::Warning is false. MarkKind::BreakpointActive is false. Branch from the current tip of main. base_sha records that tip at planning time. If main has moved, use the new tip. Keep the change under about 60 lines. Stay inside this one behavior. Do not add a second case for coherence. Run the full test module named in the commands, not only the new test."
